== next (exit 0)
would run: a batch's suite that has finished (target/suite.lock/exit-<sha>): handle it (drive_settle) first; one still running: go on, CI runs it
would run: git fetch origin develop; new commits there merged into HEAD (MERGE <sha8> pulled <n> commits; scripts/*.nika among them: RESTART)
would run: df -m --output=avail /: under 6 GB free, the cleanup below; still under 3 GB after it, ESCALATE
no issue for b1
would run: write T/b1.md.running (the run's start, removed when its follow-up is done)
would run: target/fast/nikaia run scripts/agent.nika -- T/b1.md --dir T
would run: gh api repos/Nikaia-Foundation/Nikaia/issues/<issue of b1>/comments -F body=@<Run: the result, tokens, cost, time, turns, report, debrief, the footer>
would run: rewrite Pushed: in T/b1.md.report.md when its Commit: is in the log (nothing committed)
would run: append T/b1.md to T/unpushed.txt (no suite until the block or the batch ends)
would run: builder run 1 of a block of B (drive_lane_block); at B: the suite on HEAD in the background (BLOCK <n> builder runs: the suite starts), the next builders go on
DRY-RUN NEXT b1
== batch done (exit 0)
would run: rm -rf target/debug (unless a cargo in this checkout builds into it) target/nikaia-example-tests target/gate-tests-* target/pre-push-*; rm -rf each $TMPDIR/nikaia-test-<pid>-<n> whose pid is gone; NIKAIA_CACHE_DIR=target/nikaia-project-tests NIKAIA_CACHE_LIMIT=2G target/fast/nikaia cache prune; under 6 GB after it and no cargo or rustc building into target/fast or target/release, rm -rf target/fast/incremental target/release/incremental target/ledger-target/fast/incremental, and in target/fast/deps target/release/deps target/ledger-target/fast/deps rm each <name>-<16 hex><rest> last changed over 3 h ago whose <name> has a newer file of another hash; print CLEANUP freed <N> MB, <M> MB free
would run: a suite still running (target/suite.lock/testing): wait for it first (SUITE <sha8> waiting)
would run: git fetch origin develop; git rev-list --count origin/develop..HEAD (0: nothing to test)
would run: git log --format= --name-only origin/develop..HEAD: all documentation by scripts/ci-changes.sh's rule, push HEAD without the suite (SUITE <sha8> docs-only, pushed without the suite), empty T/unpushed.txt
would run: all documentation or helper scripts with named tests (drive_scripts_only): after the lock, the named tests here; green: push HEAD without the suite (SUITE <sha8> scripts-only, local tests green, pushed without the suite), empty T/unpushed.txt; red: Gate: red local-tests, QA
would run: mkdir target/suite.lock (wait while its owner's pid lives)
would run: after the lock and before each suite: git fetch origin develop; git rev-list --count origin/develop..HEAD (0: SUITE nothing new after the lock, empty T/unpushed.txt, rm -rf target/suite.lock)
would run: git push --force origin <sha>:refs/heads/ci/<last part of DIR> (the whole CI workflow runs on that push); in the background, with the compiler of HEAD (target/ledger-target/fast/nikaia, built there first unless its stamp names HEAD's crates/): run scripts/drive.nika -- --ci-wait <sha> T/suite.log target/suite.lock/exit-<sha>, its pid to target/suite.lock/wait-<sha>.pid, its stderr to wait-<sha>.err (gh api every 30 s; Gate: green, or Gate: red <failed jobs> with their log tails)
would run: builders go on meanwhile; once it has finished (or before a bump, the next suite, the end): handle it; green: git push origin <sha>:develop, drop the tested briefs from T/unpushed.txt, rm -rf target/suite.lock; then, unless --no-bump or HEAD moved past it, target/fast/nikaia run scripts/release.nika -- T (RELEASE lines) and WAKE PUSHED
would run: red: write T/qa-input.txt, mkdir -p T/qa, copy docs/qa-task.md to T/qa/qa-task.md (its report path made T/qa/qa-task.md.report.md), rm -f T/qa/qa-task.md.report.md, target/fast/nikaia run scripts/agent.nika -- T/qa/qa-task.md --dir T, its report and run files stay untracked, the suite again and waited for (at most 2 QA rounds)
would run: git fetch origin develop; new commits there merged into HEAD (MERGE <sha8> pulled <n> commits; scripts/*.nika among them: RESTART)
would run: wait for the suite (drive_settle), then stop for the supervisor (exit 2)
DRY-RUN STOP BATCH DONE
